Z||000000||jch82||10-13-2001||02:01 AM||||Well, I finally found my new fiero! She is an 84 SE 4speed with 98k miles. Has power windows and locks although the driver window doesnt work. I think the switch is bad.<P>It has been sitting for 6 months before I came and picked it up in Ann Arbor, MI. That is about a 3hr drive from my house. I'm so happy she made it all the way. Now she will get a tune-up this weekend. A badly needed one and a good cleaning!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> It has that musty 6month non-driven smell.....Only feature it has is the anti-theft decklid....  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> I have to find a new one of those. Any donors?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Also, anyone have a steel clutch pedal arm out of an 87-88?? Mine is bent all up and I think thats why I'm having trouble shifting. Thanks!!<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/IM000001(forum).jpg">  <P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/IM000003(forum).JPG">  <P>Josh   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jch82flag.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by jch82 (edited 10-13-2001).]||||reg||7
Z||000001||Dave Gunsul||10-13-2001||02:09 AM||||Woohoo Josh! Now you don't have to drive your other one through the winter.<BR>That also means that you'll be able to rip the other ones engine out this winter for a little more power while you drive this one.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Hmm, it looks like there's a lot of leaves in the engine compartment.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>(inside jk)<P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver<p>[This message has been edited by Dave Gunsul (edited 10-13-2001).]||||reg||14
Z||000002||Archie||10-13-2001||02:19 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by jch82:<BR><B><BR>Also, anyone have a steel clutch pedal arm out of an 87-88?? Mine is bent all up and I think thats why I'm having trouble shifting. Thanks!!<P>Josh    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>You don't have to mess around with installing a used Clutch pedal and you don't have to pay some Fiero Vendor for one. You can buy them NEW at your local GM dealer. This web page gives you the details. <A HREF="http://home.v8archie.com/arch7.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://home.v8archie.com/arch7.htm</A> <P>Archie||||reg||1
Z||000003||hurley_kid_87||10-13-2001||02:21 AM||||yeah you gotta watch them leaves Josh...they will get ya everytime   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">...we dont need no fieros in distress, and too bad that front end wont compare to your GT! kinda sad josh with a car without a smooth front end  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><BR>HEHE<BR>Andy<P>------------------<BR>I NEED a Fiero!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000004||tomanyfieros||10-13-2001||08:25 AM||||hey, i got a decklid, it is red, off an 84, and i think i got a switch for u, LMK, u can have hurley kid come get it when he picks up his "look a like" 85 GT to urs...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> people might wave to hurley, thinking it is u! lol glad u got it, and i got parts for u, Thanx Jason<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/dreamer.gif">    <BR><B>We all have dreams, but not everyone gets them...</B>||||reg||1
Z||000005||MooCow||10-13-2001||10:08 AM||||Josh you forgot to mention that this car lite on Fire on the way home.  I was following Josh home after picking it up and I see sparks comming from under the car.  I flash him and he looks and see's sparks flying out the broken decklid and pulls off the highway.  We looked in the engine bay through the vent and seen that leaves were on fire and quickly tried to put it out but couldn't.  so we ran away from the car and called 911 and they came with a Fire truck, but by the time they got there the leaves have all burnt up and the fire was out.  <BR>So the next time we go and buy a Fiero I am going to make sure that there are no leaves in the engine bay area.  Thank god nothing happend just a long delay on our ride home because of it.<P>Thanks Ken||||reg||1
