Z||000011||Tigger||10-13-2001||02:56 PM||||Looks pretty good, is this one going to be the next project, just a daily driver, or both?<P>First things you need to check on these SE's:<BR>- Make sure you have no valve cover leaks!<BR>- No leaves.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"><BR>- Change the plugs/wires.  Be careful changing the plugs if they are corroded bad.  Had one snap off in the head on mine but got it out.<BR>- Make sure no oil is coming from under the oil cap.<BR>- Check the PVC valve & breather.<BR>- Check the alternator belt, or just replace it.<P>Congrats on your find, make sure you post some pictures with it all cleaned up!<p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 10-13-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000012||jch82||10-14-2001||12:38 AM||||Pat: got the pics. they look great! cant wait until the euro taillights are done!! lets hope you sell lots of them to fund those rocker panels that I need before I paint my fiero.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>James: Side scoops are yours buddy. Just come and get them or I will see you sometime and then you can get them. I'll go with but I have to work Saturday. If I don't work Sunday then maybe we can go or something.<P>85 gt fiero: Sorry man! I really needed a winter beast. I'm lucky to have run across it. I'll let you know if I find any other fieros.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Tigger: I have already changed most things. Going to put the PCV valve and breather as well as belt on tomorrow. At least for this winter it will be my daily driver. Don't really want to drive the GT with all the mods I have done to the exterior. Would really suck to get in a crash! I'll get some pics when it's not raining out and she is all cleaned up.<P>Josh  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jch82flag.jpg"> ||||reg||7
